<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tuhfat al-Nafis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1865</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as The Precious Gift</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tuhfat al-Nafis ('The Precious Gift') is a Malay history of the kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riau">Riau</a>, Siak and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> written in the nineteenth century, completed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raja-ali-haji">Raja Ali Haji</a> of Riau-Lingga around 1865 from an earlier draft by his father. It traces the Malay rulers and the Bugis princes who served as viceroys in Riau from the seventeenth to the nineteenth century, and it is a leading source for the region's history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tuhfat-al-nafis.jpg" alt="Tuhfat al-Nafis" width="300" height="446" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Bugis. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tuhfat_alnafis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
